{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1879018,
  "courseSlug": "nodejs-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "NodeJS - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "20342251",
      "title": "Using the Standard Library",
      "lectureOrder": 525,
      "videoOrder": 466,
      "sourceHash": "b7c4a5d4a55e01492f8ee5909d2f0b6f73af236a35870d318138eb65dbb70e76",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.27,
          "end": 3.21,
          "en": "So let's get started",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.21,
          "end": 5.21,
          "en": "with some Standard Libraries.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.21,
          "end": 9.13,
          "en": "And for that, I'm actually going to work with",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.13,
          "end": 11.22,
          "en": "the HTTP library.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.22,
          "end": 15.14,
          "en": "That library will help us with spinning up a web server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.14,
          "end": 17.42,
          "en": "and actually here in the docs of the library,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.42,
          "end": 21.16,
          "en": "we have some dummy code for doing that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.16,
          "end": 23.68,
          "en": "So in the end, we're just going to replicate that code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.68,
          "end": 26.97,
          "en": "but I'm going to explain what's happening here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.97,
          "end": 30.92,
          "en": "Now we see one important difference to note right away",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.92,
          "end": 33.04,
          "en": "and that's the import syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.04,
          "end": 36.39,
          "en": "Now, I don't just mean the import from syntax,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.39,
          "end": 39.81,
          "en": "which differs from the const require import syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.81,
          "end": 41.46,
          "en": "we used throughout this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.46,
          "end": 45.3,
          "en": "but I also mean, from where we are importing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.3,
          "end": 47.24,
          "en": "That's a URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.24,
          "end": 51.5,
          "en": "As you learned, Node does support the import from syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.5,
          "end": 54.06,
          "en": "I do cover that in the modern JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.06,
          "end": 56.31,
          "en": "with Node core section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.31,
          "end": 60.71,
          "en": "But what Node doesn't support, are URL imports.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.71,
          "end": 65.47,
          "en": "Where we don't import from a local file or a module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.47,
          "end": 68.81,
          "en": "but where we instead point at a file on another server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.81,
          "end": 70.4,
          "en": "to import that file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.4,
          "end": 73.003,
          "en": "And that's something Deno does.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.003,
          "end": 77.26,
          "en": "Deno wants you to use such imports.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.26,
          "end": 81.25,
          "en": "The idea with Deno is not that you download everything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.25,
          "end": 84.72,
          "en": "you're going to use in your project and store it locally,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.72,
          "end": 87.68,
          "en": "but then instead, you can import from any JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.68,
          "end": 90.41,
          "en": "or TypeScript file on any server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.41,
          "end": 94.43299999999999,
          "en": "and start using those exported features in your files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.59,
          "end": 97.85,
          "en": "This is a core philosophy of Deno",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.85,
          "end": 100.82,
          "en": "and that's, of course quite different to Node.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 100.82,
          "end": 104.47999999999999,
          "en": "So therefore, here, if we want to use this standard library,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 104.47999999999999,
          "end": 107.74000000000001,
          "en": "the HTTP library, and from that library,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 107.74000000000001,
          "end": 112.1,
          "en": "the serve function exported from the server.ts file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 112.1,
          "end": 115.50999999999999,
          "en": "then we have to go into our app.ts file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 115.50999999999999,
          "end": 117.42,
          "en": "and add this code in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 117.42,
          "end": 118.95,
          "en": "And this will then do just that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 118.95,
          "end": 123.2,
          "en": "It will import a function from this remote file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 123.2,
          "end": 125.6,
          "en": "and of course you can only import what's exported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 125.6,
          "end": 128.24,
          "en": "if we dive into the server.ts file though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.24,
          "end": 131.663,
          "en": "we see that if we search for serve,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 137.82999999999998,
          "end": 139.82,
          "en": "If we search long enough, at least",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 142.75,
          "end": 145.67000000000002,
          "en": "we have the exported serve function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 145.67000000000002,
          "end": 147.44,
          "en": "because it's exported here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 147.44,
          "end": 149.453,
          "en": "we can import it with this code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 150.49,
          "end": 153.67000000000002,
          "en": "So, this is how we import and we don't need to download",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 153.67000000000002,
          "end": 158.41,
          "en": "or NPM install this, it's also not built into Deno",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 158.41,
          "end": 161.51,
          "en": "so it's also not like the file system module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 161.51,
          "end": 163.02,
          "en": "which comes with Node.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 163.02,
          "end": 165.43,
          "en": "Instead, it simply sits on another server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 165.43,
          "end": 167.49,
          "en": "and this is how we import it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 167.49,
          "end": 169.52,
          "en": "Now serve is then a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 169.52,
          "end": 173.39,
          "en": "that allows us to spin up a HTTP server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 173.39,
          "end": 176.52,
          "en": "And we spin up that server by calling serve,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 176.52,
          "end": 179.85,
          "en": "and then through serve, we pass an object to configure it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 179.85,
          "end": 181.89,
          "en": "and in this object, we can, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 181.89,
          "end": 184.36,
          "en": "specify the port on which we wanna listen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 184.36,
          "end": 187.89,
          "en": "And here for development, we could do this on port 3000.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 187.89,
          "end": 190.793,
          "en": "We do this with the port property in this object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 191.87,
          "end": 194.02,
          "en": "Now server then returns a server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 194.02,
          "end": 196.57999999999998,
          "en": "which we can store in a constant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 196.57999999999998,
          "end": 198.12,
          "en": "And now this server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 198.12,
          "end": 201.07999999999998,
          "en": "of course could have incoming requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 201.07999999999998,
          "end": 205.55,
          "en": "In Node.js, we would now specify a callback function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 205.55,
          "end": 208.05,
          "en": "that executes for every incoming request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 208.05,
          "end": 212.56,
          "en": "Deno instead embraces modern JavaScript features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 212.56,
          "end": 215.07,
          "en": "for all its core capabilities,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 215.07,
          "end": 217.7,
          "en": "and the server is no exception.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 217.7,
          "end": 219.02,
          "en": "In this example, snippet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 219.02,
          "end": 223.28,
          "en": "we see how we listen to incoming requests in Deno",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 223.28,
          "end": 227.26,
          "en": "with this strange construct here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 227.26,
          "end": 230,
          "en": "Now for await of,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 230,
          "end": 232.11,
          "en": "is a JavaScript feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 232.11,
          "end": 234.13,
          "en": "it's not Deno exclusive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 234.13,
          "end": 238.81,
          "en": "Instead, it's a JavaScript feature called async iterable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 238.81,
          "end": 242.69,
          "en": "Server, is this so called asynchronous iterable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 242.69,
          "end": 247.14,
          "en": "which simply means it's like an array full of promises",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 247.14,
          "end": 249.77,
          "en": "and it's an infinite array basically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 249.77,
          "end": 252.93,
          "en": "So this server generates new promises",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 252.93,
          "end": 255.07,
          "en": "which we can await like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 255.07,
          "end": 256.58,
          "en": "and the new promise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 256.58,
          "end": 258.48,
          "en": "which then resolves, is generated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 258.48,
          "end": 260.3,
          "en": "for every incoming request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 260.3,
          "end": 263.99,
          "en": "That's what server does under the hood, the Deno server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 263.99,
          "end": 267.41,
          "en": "And you could build this entirely with vanilla JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 267.41,
          "end": 271.033,
          "en": "async iterables are vanilla JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 271.97,
          "end": 274.92,
          "en": "Attached, you'll find a link to the MDN documentation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 274.92,
          "end": 277.7,
          "en": "for async iterables, in case you're interested",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 277.7,
          "end": 280.09000000000003,
          "en": "in learning a bit more about them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 280.09000000000003,
          "end": 282.78,
          "en": "So, if I copy this code here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 282.78,
          "end": 286.88,
          "en": "into my app.ts file, we'll execute this code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 286.88,
          "end": 288.99,
          "en": "for every incoming request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 288.99,
          "end": 293.04,
          "en": "And this is just a Deno's way of sending back a response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 293.04,
          "end": 296.21,
          "en": "on the request object which is generated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 296.21,
          "end": 297.99,
          "en": "for every incoming request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 297.99,
          "end": 300.19,
          "en": "We got a respond method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 300.19,
          "end": 303.94,
          "en": "which wants an object, where we can specify a body",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 303.94,
          "end": 307.56,
          "en": "for the response, which will be sent back by Deno.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 307.56,
          "end": 309.63,
          "en": "So this is how we listen to requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 309.63,
          "end": 313.7,
          "en": "then do whatever we wanna do, and then respond back.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 313.7,
          "end": 316.35,
          "en": "And one noteworthy thing here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 316.35,
          "end": 321.25,
          "en": "is that we have await here, on the top level like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 321.25,
          "end": 324.87,
          "en": "This is not wrapped in any asynchronous function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 324.87,
          "end": 327.31,
          "en": "as you often needed in Avro code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 327.31,
          "end": 332.22,
          "en": "instead Deno out of the box supports top level await.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 332.22,
          "end": 334.65,
          "en": "So that you can use the await keyword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 334.65,
          "end": 337.05,
          "en": "outside of asynchronous functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 337.05,
          "end": 339.44,
          "en": "In modern versions of Node.js,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 339.44,
          "end": 341.45,
          "en": "this is also supported though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 341.45,
          "end": 343.563,
          "en": "so that's not really a key difference.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 344.44,
          "end": 347.79,
          "en": "Well, with that, if we save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 347.79,
          "end": 351.46,
          "en": "if I now run this file with Deno run app.ts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 351.46,
          "end": 355.28,
          "en": "it compiles and it will ultimately crash,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 355.28,
          "end": 356.75,
          "en": "but before it crashes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 356.75,
          "end": 359.54,
          "en": "you see it downloads a bunch of things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 359.54,
          "end": 362.46,
          "en": "And that happens because of this import.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 362.46,
          "end": 365.46,
          "en": "Whenever you import from a URL like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 365.46,
          "end": 367.016,
          "en": "when you execute the code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 367.016,
          "end": 370.12,
          "en": "Deno goes ahead and reaches out to that server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 370.12,
          "end": 371.88,
          "en": "and downloads that file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 371.88,
          "end": 374.64,
          "en": "and of course, also dependencies of that file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 374.64,
          "end": 378.37,
          "en": "So, all other files which are imported by that file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 378.37,
          "end": 381.6,
          "en": "and it downloads those files to your local machine,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 381.6,
          "end": 383.7,
          "en": "and caches them locally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 383.7,
          "end": 386.41,
          "en": "so that when you run the script thereafter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 386.41,
          "end": 388.46,
          "en": "it doesn't have to re-download them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 388.46,
          "end": 390.84,
          "en": "simply to speed up execution time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 390.84,
          "end": 394.69,
          "en": "and to make sure it doesn't exhaust all your bandwidth.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 394.69,
          "end": 398.2,
          "en": "With this approach, you can also develop on a plane,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 398.2,
          "end": 401.74,
          "en": "assuming that you did pre-download all the files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 401.74,
          "end": 402.993,
          "en": "you'll eventually need.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 405.97,
          "end": 408.87,
          "en": "Now, after it did all that, it crashes however,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 408.87,
          "end": 412.11,
